(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_zoology_reproductivehealth=[{id:"neet-2026-q138",pn:138,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Assisted reproductive technologies",q:"Choose the correct statement regarding GIFT to overcome infertility.",o:["Ova collected from a female donor are transferred to the uterus of an infertile female.","It is the transfer of an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce ovum but can provide suitable environment for fertilization and development.","Early embryos with up to 8 blastomeres are transferred to the uterus of an infertile female.","Early embryos with up to 8 blastomeres are transferred into the fallopian tube of an infertile female."],c:1,s:`GIFT is an in-vivo technique used to assist infertility.
GIFT (Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer) transfers an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce one but can provide a suitable environment for fertilization and further development.
ZIFT (Zygote Intra Fallopian Transfer) is an in-vitro technique in which the zygote or early embryo up to 8 blastomeres is transferred into the fallopian tube.`},{id:"neet-2026-q147",pn:147,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods",q:`Match List I and List II
A. Progestasert \u2014 I. Barrier made of rubber used by females
B. Multiload 375 \u2014 II. Oral contraceptive
C. Diaphragm \u2014 III. Hormone releasing IUD
D. Saheli \u2014 IV. Copper releasing IUD`,o:["A(III), B(IV), C(I), D(II)","A(III), B(IV), C(II), D(I)","A(IV), B(II), C(I), D(III)","A(IV), B(III), C(I), D(II)"],c:0,s:`Progestasert is a hormone releasing IUD.
Multiload 375 is a copper releasing IUD.
Diaphragm is a barrier made of rubber used by females.
Saheli is an oral contraceptive.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q171",pn:171,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Assisted reproductive technologies",q:"The method of directly of injecting a sperm into ovum in assisted reproductive technology is called:",o:["Zygote intra fallopian transfer (ZIFT)","Intra cytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI)","Embryo transfer (ET)","Gamete intra fallopian transfer (GIFT)"],c:1,s:`ICSI is a procedure to form an embryo in the laboratory in which a sperm is injected directly into the ovum.
ZIFT transfers the zygote or early embryo (up to 8 blastomeres) into the fallopian tube.
GIFT transfers an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce one but can give a suitable environment for fertilisation and development.`},{id:"neet-2025-q093",pn:93,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Assisted reproductive technologies, IVF",q:`What are the potential drawbacks in adoption of the IVF method?
A. High fatality risk to mother
B. Expensive instruments and reagents
C. Husband/wife necessary for being donors
D. Less adoption of orphans
E. Not available in India
F. Possibility that the early embryo does not survive
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["B, D, F only","A, C, D, F only","A, B, C, D only","A, B, C, E, F only"],c:0,s:`Statements B, D and F are correct.
Statements A, C and E are incorrect.
Husband/wife is not necessary for being donors. IVF is available in India.`},{id:"neet-2024-q152",pn:152,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods (IUDs)",q:`Match List I with List II :
A. Non-medicated IUD \u2014 I. Multiload 375
B. Copper releasing IUD \u2014 II. Progestogens
C. Hormone releasing IND \u2014 III. Lippes loop
D. Implants \u2014 IV. LNG-20
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV","A-I, B-III, C-IV, D-II"],c:1,s:`Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD.
Multiload 375 is a copper releasing IUD.
LNG-20 is a hormone releasing IUD.
Progestogens are used as implants.
So A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II.`},{id:"neet-2024-q175",pn:175,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods",q:"Which of the following is not a natural/traditional contraceptive method?",o:["Lactational amenorrhea","Vaults","Coitus interruptus","Periodic abstinence"],c:1,s:`Option (2) is correct.
A vault is a rubber barrier method placed in the female tract to cover the cervix during coitus.
Lactational amenorrhea is natural: ovulation and cycles do not occur during intense lactation after childbirth.
Coitus interruptus is natural: the male withdraws before ejaculation.
Periodic abstinence is natural: couples avoid coitus in the fertile period.`},{id:"neet-2023-q152",pn:152,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"RCH programme and amniocentesis",q:`Given below are two statement : one is labeled as Assertion A and the other is labeled as Reason R.
Assertion A : Amniocentesis for sex determination is one of the strategies of Reproductive and Child Health Care Programme.
Reason R : Ban on amniocentesis checks increasing menace of female foeticide.
In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.`,o:["A is false but R is true.","Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.","Both A and R are true and R is NOT the correct explanation of A.","A is true but R is false"],c:0,s:`The RCH programme spreads awareness about reproduction and gives facilities and support for a reproductively healthy society.
Amniocentesis is used to test for genetic disorders such as Down's syndrome and haemophilia, and to judge whether the foetus can survive.
It is not a sex determination method in India and not an RCH strategy, so A is false.
R is true: the ban on it checks female foeticide.`},{id:"neet-2023-q168",pn:168,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Sexually transmitted infections",q:"Which one of the following common sexually transmitted diseases is completely curable when detected early and treated properly ?",o:["HIV Infection","Genital herpes","Gonorrhoea","Hepatitis-B"],c:2,s:`Apart from hepatitis-B, genital herpes and HIV infection, other STIs are completely curable if found early and treated well.
Gonorrhoea is bacterial and can be cured.
The other three are viral.`},{id:"neet-2023-q185",pn:185,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods",q:`Match List I with List II.
List I: A. Vasectomy; B. Coitus interruptus; C. Cervical caps; D. Saheli
List II: I. Oral method; II. Barrier method; III. Surgical method; IV. Natural method
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A-IV, B-II, C-I, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV"],c:2,s:`Vasectomy is a surgical method.
Coitus interruptus is a natural method.
Cervical cap is a barrier method.
Saheli is an oral, non-steroidal pill.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q153",pn:153,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods IUDs",q:"Which of the following is not an Intra Uterine Device?",o:["Progestasert","Progestogens","Multiload 375","Lippes loop"],c:1,s:`IUDs are of three kinds.
Non-medicated: Lippes loop.
Copper releasing: CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375.
Hormone releasing: Progestasert, LNG-20.
Progestogens are hormones, not a device.`},{id:"neet-2022-q172",pn:172,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Intrauterine devices",q:"Lippe's loop is a type of contraceptive used as:",o:["Vault barrier","Non-Medicated IUD","Copper releasing IUD","Cervical barrier"],c:1,s:`Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD.
Copper-releasing IUDs are CuT, Cu7 and multiload 375.
Diaphragms, cervical caps and vaults are barrier methods.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q193",pn:193,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods: IUDs",q:`IUDs are small objects made up of plastic or copper that are inserted in the uterine cavity. Which of the following statements are correct about IUDs?
(a) IUDs decrease phagocytosis of sperm within the uterus.
(b) The released copper ions suppress the sperm motility.
(c) IUDs do not make the cervix hostile to the sperm.
(d) IUDs suppress the fertilization capacity of sperm.
(e) The IUDs require surgical intervention for their insertion in the uterine cavity.
Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:`,o:["(d) only","(a), (d) and (e) only","(b) and (c) only","(b) and (d) only"],c:3,s:`A doctor or trained nurse inserts an IUD through the vagina; no surgery is needed, so (e) is false.
IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperm, so (a) is false.
They make the cervix hostile to sperm, so (c) is false.
Copper ions reduce sperm motility and fertilising capacity, so (b) and (d) are true.`},{id:"neet-2022-q200",pn:200,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraception methods",q:"Match List \u2013 I with List \u2013 II with respect to methods of contraception and their respective actions. (a) Diaphragms (b) Contraceptive Pills (c) Intra Uterine Devices (d) Lactational Amenorrhea ; (i) Inhibit ovulation and implantation (ii) Increase phagocytosis of sperm within Uterus (iii) Absence of Menstural cycle and ovulation following parturition (iv) They cove the cervix blocking the entry of sperms",o:["(a) - (iv), (b) - (i), (c) - (ii), (d) - (iii)","(a) - (ii), (b) - (iv), (c) - (i), (d) - (iii)","(a) - (iii), (b) - (ii), (c) - (i), (d) - (iv)","(a) - (iv), (b) - (i), (c) - (iii), (d) - (ii)"],c:0,s:`Diaphragms are barriers that cover the cervix and block sperm entry.
Pills (progestogen or progestogen with oestrogen) inhibit ovulation and implantation and thicken cervical mucus.
IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperm in the uterus.
Lactational amenorrhoea: no ovulation or periods during intense lactation after childbirth.
So a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii.`},{id:"neet-2021-q166",pn:166,y:"NEET 2021 \xB7 12 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Sexually transmitted diseases",q:`Veneral diseases can spread through :
(a) Using sterile needles (b) Transfusion of blood from infected person (c) Infected mother to foetus (d) Kissing (e) Inheritance`,o:["(a) and (c) only","(a), (b) and (c) only","(b), (c) and (d) only","(b) and (c) only"],c:3,s:`Sexually transmitted infections spread by sharing infected needles, by blood transfusion and from an infected mother to her foetus.
(a) says sterile needles, which do not spread infection.
Kissing and inheritance do not spread them.
So only (b) and (c).`},{id:"neet-2021-q174",pn:174,y:"NEET 2021 \xB7 12 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods",q:`Match List-I with List-II.
List-I: (a) Vaults (b) IUDs (c) Vasectomy (d) Tubectomy
List-II: (i) Entry of sperm through Cervix is blocked (ii) Removal of Vas deferens (iii) Phagocytosis of sperms within the Uterus (iv) Removal of fallopian tube`,o:["(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)","(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iiii)","(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)","(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)"],c:2,s:`Vaults are barriers over the cervix, blocking sperm entry: a-i.
IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperm in the uterus: b-iii.
Vasectomy removes (or ties) part of the vas deferens: c-ii.
Tubectomy removes (or ties) part of the fallopian tube: d-iv.`},{id:"neet-2021-q181",pn:181,y:"NEET 2021 \xB7 12 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"IUDs",q:"Which one of the following is an example of Hormone releasing IUD?",o:["Multiload 375","CuT","LNG 20","Cu 7"],c:2,s:`LNG-20 releases the hormone levonorgestrel.
Multiload 375, CuT and Cu7 are copper-releasing IUDs.`},{id:"neet-2021-q194",pn:194,y:"NEET 2021 \xB7 12 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"MOET in cattle",q:"Which of the following is not a step in Multiple Ovulation Embryo Transfer Technology (MOET)?",o:["Fertilized eggs are transferred to surrogate mothers at 8-32 cell stage","Cow is administered hormone having LH like activity for super ovulation","Cow yields about 6-8 eggs at a time","Cow is fertilized by artificial insemination"],c:1,s:`In MOET the cow is given a hormone with FSH-like activity (not LH-like) to cause superovulation.
She yields 6-8 eggs, is mated or artificially inseminated, and the 8-32 cell embryos are moved to surrogate mothers.
So statement 2 is the wrong step.`},{id:"neet-2020-q025",pn:25,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Assisted reproductive technologies",q:"In which of the following techniques, the embryos are transferred to assist those females who cannot conceive ?",o:["GIFT and ZIFT","ICSI and ZIFT","GIFT and ICSI","ZIFT and IUT"],c:3,s:`In ZIFT the zygote or early embryo (up to 8 blastomeres) is moved into the fallopian tube.
In IUT embryos with more than 8 blastomeres are moved into the uterus.
So the embryo-transfer methods are ZIFT and IUT.`},{id:"neet-2020-q028",pn:28,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Sexually transmitted infections",q:"Select the option including all sexually transmitted diseases.",o:["Gonorrhoea, Malaria, Genital herpes","AIDS, Malaria, Filaria","Cancer, AIDS, Syphilis","Gonorrhoea, Syphilis, Genital herpes"],c:3,s:`Gonorrhoea, syphilis and genital herpes are STDs.
Malaria and filaria are vector-borne and cancer is not infectious.`},{id:"neet-2019-q040",pn:40,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraception",q:"Which of the following contraceptive methods do involve a role of hormone?",o:["CuT, Pills, Emergency contraceptives","Pills, Emergency contraceptives, Barrier methods","Lactational amenorrhea, Pills, Emergency contraceptives","Barrier method, Lactational amenorrhea, Pills"],c:2,s:`Pills and emergency contraceptives contain hormones.
In lactational amenorrhea, hormones of lactation stop ovulation.
CuT and barrier methods do not use hormones.`},{id:"neet-2019-q061",pn:61,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Sexually transmitted infections",q:"Which of the following sexually transmitted diseases is not completely curable ?",o:["Genital herpes","Chlamydiasis","Gonorrhoea","Genital warts"],c:0,s:`Chlamydiasis and gonorrhoea are bacterial and can be cured with antibiotics.
Genital herpes is viral and is not completely curable.`},{id:"neet-2019-q084",pn:84,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraception",q:"Select the horomone-releasing Intra-Uterine Devices.",o:["Progestasert, LNG-20","Lippes Loop, Multiload 375","Vaults, LNG-20","Multiload 375, Progestasert"],c:0,s:`Progestasert and LNG-20 release hormones.
Lippes Loop is non-medicated and Multiload 375 releases copper.
Vaults are not IUDs.`},{id:"neet-2018-q137",pn:137,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive Saheli",q:"The contraceptive 'SAHELI'",o:["blocks estrogen receptors in the uterus, preventing eggs from getting implanted.","increases the concentration of estrogen and prevents ovulation in females.","is an IUD","is a post-coital contraceptive."],c:0,s:`Saheli is a once-a-week non-steroidal oral pill developed in India.
It blocks estrogen receptors in the uterus, so implantation is prevented.
It is not an IUD and not a post-coital pill.`}]})();
